WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.336
- You know,  I'm a seven-footer 
that plays with a lot of anger

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.547
and, you know, people don't have that
vision of me crying.

00:00:06.214 --> 00:00:09.092
- Do the aliens know
that we exist?

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:11.344
- Do you think my best friend's an alien?

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:14.806
If you just wanna believe the easy answer
to make you feel better,

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:16.850
like most people do,
then fine.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.068
- More travel.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:32.699
We're in the airport because I'm heading to Utah
for my first-ever time in the state.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.286
But I'm not going to be skiing. I'm going
to interview big man Rudy Gobert.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.247
He was wildly made fun of
on social media

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:42.751
when he shed some tears after
not making the All-Star Game,

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:47.672
but then he ended the season breaking
the all-time single-season dunk record.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.093
So now we're off to Swat Lake City
to learn more about him.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.640
You coordinated very well
for this shoot.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.147
So on Instagram, you commented
on a photo,

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:05.148
or a video,

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:08.276
of Joel Embiid saying that he was the
best defensive player in the league

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:10.445
and the most unstoppable
player in the league.

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.322
You put laughing emojis.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.199
Why was that funny?

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.534
- Because of his accent.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.578
- That's why it was funny.
- Yeah.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.455
- Had nothing to do with
what he said?

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:21.581
- Um...yeah, what he said.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.792
I mean, it's almost like every interview,

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.169
he tries to say that he's
the best defensive player in the league.

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:27.754
You don't need to say it
every interview, you know.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:33.051
People are gonna look at the stats and 
look at the numbers and judge for themselves.

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:37.263
- Are you the best defensive player
in the league?

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.598
- For you, how do you judge?

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.435
Is it the guy that makes his team better?
Or the impact?

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.146
I mean, I think it's a mix of both.
- It is. I would say it's the impact,

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:46.606
the impact that you have defensively.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.774
- Yeah.
So yeah, I think I am.

00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:54.447
- So every show I have a segment
where I have a guest take me to

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.867
that moment, that time,
that person, whatever the case may be.

00:01:57.867 --> 00:01:59.869
All righty?
- OK.

00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:03.331
- Take me to how you picked
your jersey number 27.

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:07.669
- I got drafted 27th. I was a little frustrated,
to be drafted so low,

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:14.008
so I thought it was a great reminder, to myself,
and to everyone that kinda didn't draft me.

00:02:14.008 --> 00:02:16.511
- Do you know everyone that was drafted
before you?

00:02:16.511 --> 00:02:18.930
- All of them?
That's 26 guys.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:24.727
- Anthony Bennett. Victor Oladipo. Otto Porter.
Cody Zeller. Ben McLemore.

00:02:24.727 --> 00:02:27.647
Steven Adams.
[List of names speeding up]

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:33.820
- I might forget a
few ones.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.283
- Take me to a walk through the
mountains around your home.

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:41.327
- Yeah, when I moved here, you know,
I really–

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.747
the mountains were a big part of,
a big reason why I chose this home.

00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:48.918
You know, it was very private.
I really like the views,

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:51.546
you know and I like to
go hiking.

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:56.092
- So when you said you got drafted to Utah
and you're like 'What is Utah?'–

00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:58.511
did you envision this being Utah?

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.306
- I never really been around
mountains like that, so no.

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:06.102
- Have you gone skiing?
- I never skied in my life.

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:07.687
- Maybe snowboard.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.731
- Snowball?
- Snowboard.

00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:12.400
- Snowball fighting?
- I did snowballs before, yes,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.485
but snowboard.

00:03:14.485 --> 00:03:16.112
- Snowball fighting?

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:18.615
- Is my English that bad?

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.450
- No, I just didn't hear what you said.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.787
- Snowboard.
- Snowboard! Snowboard, snowboard. I'm sorry.

00:03:24.787 --> 00:03:26.831
- That's what I just said.
That's exactly what I just said.

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:29.542
- You needed to do, like, "snowboard"
and the motion.

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.592
- [Announcer]:
As Gobert denies Brown.

00:03:37.592 --> 00:03:40.220
- Where did NBA defense go?

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:44.724
- You know, it's like a lot of animals that
are going extinct. It's kinda the same.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:48.686
You know, I just think people are more focusing
on individual performance

00:03:48.686 --> 00:03:49.979
more than winning.

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:51.606
- You're a defensive minded guy, and

00:03:51.606 --> 00:03:55.485
so I think that you always kinda lean towards
players that play good defense.

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:57.612
Who should be the MVP?

00:03:57.612 --> 00:04:01.324
- I'm a defensive minded guy., but I'm a
winning-minded guy.

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:05.411
You know, I like the guys that do all of the little
things that helps your team win.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:08.289
We focus too much on the points and,
you know,

00:04:08.289 --> 00:04:12.460
not necessarily on the guy that
created the action or the guy that set the screen.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.964
- So who should win MVP?

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:17.966
- Who should win MVP?
If I had to vote,

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:22.345
I would pick Giannis, just because
he plays a little more defense

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:25.682
and the impact that he has.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.519
- Do you talk a lot of trash on the court?

00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:31.771
- A little bit.
- Did you talk to Giannis?

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.774
- I tried to learn some
bad words in Greek.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.234
- What words did you learn?

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.195
- Malaka.
- Which is?

00:04:39.195 --> 00:04:42.865
- I don't wanna say.
- You just said it in Greek!

00:04:42.865 --> 00:04:45.994
- And then there's a way to say, like,
"You off" or, like, "You're gonna miss."

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:47.287
I think it's "exo."

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.914
So every free throw, I was like,
"Exo, exo."

00:04:49.914 --> 00:04:52.333
- Did he look at you like, "How are you
speaking Greek?"

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:56.170
- The first time he gave me a little look.
Didn't work. No.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:01.426
- So how often do you think about,
this past All-Star?

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.306
- I don't really—
I wouldn't say that I think about it.

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:08.558
- But you feel as though you
should have been an All-Star?

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:12.353
And I mean, I understand you were not thinking
about it every day, but that was a moment for you.

00:05:12.353 --> 00:05:14.147
Like, a very frustrating moment for you.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:19.027
- You know, it's human nature, you know
to be disappointed or be frustrated.

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:23.197
But it's always, you know, how you
bounce back, and how you react to that.

00:05:23.197 --> 00:05:26.451
- Were you surprised at the reactions to that?

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:30.288
- Not really surprised. Sometimes you cry,
you don't even know why.

00:05:30.288 --> 00:05:33.750
And just because of the perception
people have of me–you know,

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:36.044
I'm a seven-footer,
that plays with a lot of anger and,

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:39.130
you know, people don't have that
vision of me crying.

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:42.508
- Rudy, we love you!
Love you.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.596
- Oh my goodness.

00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:51.684
This is why you should get a dog.
- I'd get a dog.

00:05:53.227 --> 00:05:55.855
- What up number 270?
- What's up?

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:56.939
- Yeah?

00:05:56.939 --> 00:05:59.525
- 275.
- Nice.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.027
- Thank you.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:07.784
- It's really cool, like, everyone we passed
knows that you just broke the dunk record.

00:06:07.784 --> 00:06:11.829
Like, I don't know if it's like that in every city that–
he knew the exact number.

00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:17.168
- No, it's great. We really have some
great fans, and they really embrace who we are.

00:06:19.003 --> 00:06:24.842
- So I'm curious, because you are somebody who,
in a lot of ways, embodies different identities, right?

00:06:24.842 --> 00:06:27.512
Like, you're French. You're black.

00:06:27.512 --> 00:06:29.472
- I'm kind of a mix of everything, so,
you know–

00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:33.309
- Yeah.
How, I mean, how do you identify?

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:39.357
- As a human being, you know as
a citizen of Earth, I would say.

00:06:39.357 --> 00:06:42.318
You know, I'm proud. My dad's black.
My mom is white.

00:06:42.318 --> 00:06:44.237
And I'm very proud of my black side.
I'm very proud of my white side.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.363
I'm proud of who I am.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:53.037
- You had a tweet where you were defending
the places that were called "shithole countries."

00:06:53.037 --> 00:06:54.497
Do you remember this tweet?

00:06:54.497 --> 00:06:55.748
- Yeah, I do.
- OK.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.584
So you said, "Do you know what
it means to have dreams?

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.586
To actually have to
work for something?

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:05.383
Does the fact that I left France to come
chase my dream here make France a shithole?

00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:07.677
Or does that just apply to
African countries?"

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:13.307
- Like, us, you know, the big countries, like,
the top-of-the-world countries,

00:07:13.307 --> 00:07:15.810
we actually, you know, take
a lot of resources from them.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:20.690
We don't allow them to develop, so then
we call them shithole countries.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.943
But let them develop, let them have
their own, you know leaders,

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.446
and then I think it's a
different story.

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:32.910
One day I was running, I was running here,
and I saw a snake in front of me.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.829
I just went home, went back home.

00:07:34.829 --> 00:07:37.540
- You saw the snake and turned around?
- Yeah, I turned around right away.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.584
I saw the snake, turned around,
went home.

00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:43.337
- How big was the snake?
- Not too big, but it's just, like, this–

00:07:43.337 --> 00:07:49.635
- You know what, Rudy? Like, I think you
get kinda scared easily by things.

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.220
- I'm scared of snakes.
I don't care how big it is.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:56.392
- Spiders?
- I don't like them, but I'm not scared of them.

00:07:56.392 --> 00:07:59.228
- Do you, like, let out a little scream
when you see insects?

00:07:59.228 --> 00:08:01.022
- I jump.
- You jump?

00:08:01.022 --> 00:08:02.023
- When I saw that snake–

00:08:02.023 --> 00:08:06.611
- It's just funny that someone so tall
would be scared of something so small.

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:09.447
- Yeah, it's like the elephant
and the mouse.

00:08:09.447 --> 00:08:12.617
- I know that one thing a lot of people
don't know about you is that

00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:15.620
you are very big into
conspiracy theories.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.914
- Here we go.
- Here we go.

00:08:17.914 --> 00:08:18.915
- I knew she was gonna
talk about it.

00:08:18.915 --> 00:08:22.543
- When did you first get into
exploring conspiracy theories?

00:08:22.543 --> 00:08:26.464
- I think when I was, like,
15 I started to look–

00:08:26.464 --> 00:08:27.465
- Really?

00:08:27.465 --> 00:08:30.885
- To really question things and, you know,
there's a lot of things that are wrong,

00:08:30.885 --> 00:08:34.430
and there's a lot of things that are
right on the internet, but I like the

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.143
fact that you can, you know, research and kinda
make your own idea of, you know,

00:08:39.143 --> 00:08:42.188
what you think is true and
what you think is not.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:46.859
- I just think it's really interesting because
conspiracy theories are just

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:49.820
thoughts that are out of the norm
and something you're genuinely passionate about.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:54.242
Like, you spend a lot of your time,
trying to learn things that you're unsure of.

00:08:54.242 --> 00:08:57.495
- The thing I don't–I don't really like
the term "conspiracy theory" because it

00:08:57.495 --> 00:09:01.874
makes it look like it's negative to actually
question things when I think it's a positive thing.

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:05.670
If you're about to question things, don't
believe that it's true just because one person

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:10.675
tells you, or because you've been
taught since you were a kid that this is true.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:12.635
- What should we call them instead
of conspiracy theories?

00:09:12.635 --> 00:09:16.097
What would you call it, just so
we can have that term?

00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:20.142
- Questions.
- Questions. You believe in questioning.

00:09:20.142 --> 00:09:21.143
- I believe in questioning.

00:09:22.853 --> 00:09:24.564
- Give me your 
thoughts on aliens.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:26.357
- I believe there's 
something else.

00:09:26.357 --> 00:09:30.194
- I will say, this is one I can get behind.
I believe that there are aliens.

00:09:30.194 --> 00:09:33.406
- Yeah.
- I just think statistically, numbers-wise

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:36.284
it's much more unlikely for
us to be the only people.

00:09:36.284 --> 00:09:39.495
- Do you think–do you think they're
down on Earth, aliens on Earth?

00:09:39.495 --> 00:09:43.332
- I don't think there are aliens on Earth.
Do you think there are aliens on Earth?

00:09:43.332 --> 00:09:47.128
- I think it's possible.
We don't even know what we are, really.

00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:48.588
I mean, what are we?

00:09:48.588 --> 00:09:51.132
- So if these aliens are on Earth,
what do they look like?

00:09:51.507 --> 00:09:52.842
What are they doing?

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:56.137
Is it, like, someone in this room
could be an alien?

00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:59.307
- Yeah, probably. It comes down to you believe
what you wanna believe

00:09:59.307 --> 00:10:01.475
and you ask yourself what
you wanna ask yourself.

00:10:01.475 --> 00:10:05.062
If you just wanna believe the easy answer
to make you feel better,

00:10:05.062 --> 00:10:07.273
like most people do,
then it's fine.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:10.484
- Do the aliens know that we exist?

00:10:10.484 --> 00:10:14.196
- Do you think my best friend's an alien?
Why do you ask me like I know?

00:10:14.196 --> 00:10:16.699
You can do your show
with an alien next time.

00:10:16.699 --> 00:10:19.201
- "Take It There" with an alien?

00:10:19.201 --> 00:10:20.202
- That'd be a first.

00:10:20.202 --> 00:10:21.704
- What would you ask an alien?

00:10:21.704 --> 00:10:22.705
- If he likes basketball.

00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:25.458
- [Laughing]

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:29.920
- If he watch
"Take It There with Taylor Rooks."

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.423
- That's the best question
of them all.

00:10:35.343 --> 00:10:37.470
You know what I wanna do when
I get up here?

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.263
I just wanna yell.

00:10:39.263 --> 00:10:42.183
- Go ahead.
You have the worst ideas ever.

00:10:42.183 --> 00:10:44.435
- I'm the king of the world!

00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:47.438
Swat Lake, let's yell it.

00:10:47.438 --> 00:10:48.773
- Swat Lake?
- Swat Lake.

00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:51.233
- Not "Take It There"?
- But really yell, OK?

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:52.234
On three.

00:10:52.234 --> 00:10:55.655
One–don't hang me
out to dry.

00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:57.490
Two, three.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.201
- Swat Lake!

00:11:00.201 --> 00:11:01.327
- Didn't that feel good?

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:03.454
I would come out here and
yell every day.

00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:07.416
- I've been here six years.
I've never thought about coming and yelling.

00:11:07.416 --> 00:11:08.417
- But wasn't it liberating?

00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:09.835
- It was really–you're too crazy.

00:11:11.045 --> 00:11:11.879
- Bein' extra.

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.173
I don't have long enough arms to do it.

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:15.800
Can you take it?
-Yep.

00:11:16.717 --> 00:11:17.718
- Put up the camera.

00:11:17.718 --> 00:11:18.719
- Your hair. Fix your hair.

00:11:18.719 --> 00:11:20.763
- You're right, my hair doesn't look good.
You're right.

00:11:20.763 --> 00:11:22.515
- There we go.
- There we go.

00:11:22.515 --> 00:11:26.686
- So I had a great time,
"Take It There with Taylor Rooks."

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:27.937
Excited to watch it.

00:11:27.937 --> 00:11:29.522
- And look, Bleacher Report's
in your house.

